	)
	(text_box "LMR51625YDDCR (2.5 A; a bay draws ≤ 2.2 A): 1.1 MHz, PFM at light load, spread spectrum.  TI SLUSF64B table 8-1 (5 V, 1.1 MHz):\n  L 4.7 µH (FXL0630, 9 A sat);  COUT 3 × 22 µF/25 V (≥ 33 µF left after DC-bias derating);  CIN 2 × 10 µF/50 V + 100 nF;  CB 100 nF.\n  At 2.2 A from 28 V the inductor peaks at ≈ 2.6 A (0.8 A ripple), under the 2.9 A minimum peak current limit.\nFB 100k/18k: VOUT = 0.8 V × (1 + 100/18) = 5.24 V: ≈ 4.75 V still reaches the DATA board at 1.4 A over 50 cm\n  of PH lead (switch, shunt, one PH pin each way); everything on +5V takes it (TJA1462AT ≤ 5.5 V).\nEN 100k/10k: the buck starts above 13.5 V and stops below 10.8 V (VEN 1.226 V, 0.241 V hysteresis), so no node\n  draws its low-voltage inrush while the hub's eFuse is soft-starting the row.\nLayout: C4/C2/C3 straddle U1's VIN and GND pins on the top layer; CIN, U1 and COUT share one top-side GND island\n  with vias to the In1 plane; the FB divider sits at the FB pin, its +5V sense comes from COUT on another layer.\nInput: SUD50P06 P-FET (reverse polarity, Vgs clamped by the 12 V zener); SMBJ33A clamps hot-plug ringing below 54 V (U1: 63 V abs max).\nVRACK is 20 V, or 28 V (EPR), from the hub's USB-C PD supply: SMBJ33A stands off 33 V (28 V + 5 % = 29.4 V), the buck runs\n  4.3–60 V and starts above 13.5 V, the P-FET and the zener clamp are rated 60 V / 12 V.  At 20 V a row draws more current: ≤ 1.6 A."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 162.56 0)
		(size 279.4 31.75)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type dash)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
